  "name": "ABSOULTE ATYPICAL LYMPHOCYTE COUNT",
  "code": "1528",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p><strong>COMMENTS:</strong><br>&middot; Atypical lymphocytes are associated with viral/bacterial infections. They may be associated with other conditions which include autoimmune<br>disorders (rheumatoid arthritis), drug reaction or medications, immunization, stress and some hormonal disorders.<br>&middot; Exposure to radiation is another cause of atypical lymphocytes.<br>&middot; Viral diseases like cytomegalovirus, Epstein Barr Virus and Hepatitis C are common causes of atypical lymphocytes.<br>&middot; Bacterial infections like toxoplasmosis, syphilis and streptococcal infections can also stimulate the formation of atypical lymphocytes.</p>",
